course: dictionary
lesson: 13178
title: Slang: freaking out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are slang, informal words that friends and older people use in everyday talk. You will hear them on TV and in conversation even if you would not use them at school. «My sister was freaking out before her test.» The words around it give the meaning: she was very worried and scared.
explain: Freaking is much milder than the rude word it can stand in for, but it is still rough slang. Do not use it in school writing or when talking to people you don't know well. If you are unsure, ask a grown-up.
explain: The verb freak can also mean to scare or upset someone. «The loud bang freaked the cat, and it ran under the bed.» Check the sentence: if your meaning fits, you have understood it.
fact: Freaking is a slang word, mostly heard in the United States and Canada, and now used in many countries.
fact: «Freak out» means to become very scared, upset or excited: «Don't freak out, it's only a spider.»
fact: «Freaking» can add strong feeling, as in «It's freaking cold!», but it is mild swearing, so it is not for school or polite company.
fact: As a verb, «freak» can mean to scare or upset someone: «The scary film freaked me out.»
fact: The forms of the verb are freak, freaks, freaked and freaking.
exercise: «The thunder was so loud that Mia freaked out and hid.» What does freaked out mean here? | * Became very scared | Went shopping | Laughed happily at the storm | Fell fast asleep
exercise: «It's freaking cold today!» What is freaking doing in this sentence? | Asking a question | Naming a place | * Adding strong feeling, as mild slang | Showing the time
exercise: Which form of freak is in «They are freaking out about the test»? | freaks | freak | * freaking | freaked
test: «The surprise party freaked her out in a happy way.» What does freaked out mean here? | Bored her | Made her sleepy | Scared her badly | * Excited her very much
test: Why should you not use freaking in your school story? | Because it is a French word | Because it means the same as cold | Because it is too short | * Because it is rough slang and not for school writing
exam: Is freaking good to use in school writing? | Yes, because it makes writing exciting | Yes, because teachers love slang | No, because it only means cold | * No, because it is rough slang and not for school writing
